---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const home = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Terms of Use | Study Hub"
  description="Terms for using Study Hub’s learning resources, document reader, AI study tools, and contribution features."
>
  <main class="legal-page">
    <header class="legal-page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Using the learning library</p>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p>These terms explain the basic conditions for using Study Hub’s website, resources, and learning tools.</p>
      <p class="policy-updated">Last updated <time datetime="2026-10-14">October 14, 2026</time></p>
    </header>

    <article class="legal-copy">
      <section>
        <h2>1. About the service</h2>
        <p>Study Hub provides a public educational resource library, document-reading features, and optional study tools. The service supports independent learning and revision. It is not a school, examining body, or substitute for instruction from a qualified teacher or official academic requirements.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Learning materials and accuracy</h2>
        <p>Resources are supplied for educational use. Syllabuses, examination requirements, descriptions, and available files can change, and materials may contain errors or be incomplete. Check important academic requirements with your school and the relevant education authorities.</p>
        <p>Study Hub may update, restrict, move, or remove pages and resources to maintain the service or respond to a rights, safety, or operational concern. The site may be temporarily unavailable, and uninterrupted access is not guaranteed.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>Use Study Hub lawfully and without disrupting the service or other visitors. Do not attempt unauthorized access, interfere with site security or operation, misuse forms or tools, distribute malware, or use the service to violate another person’s rights.</p>
        <p>Do not copy, sell, republish, or distribute a resource unless you have permission or applicable law allows it. A resource being available in the library does not itself grant a licence to reuse it.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Resource contributions</h2>
        <p>Submit only materials you have the right to share. By submitting a resource for consideration, you confirm that you are permitted to provide it and allow Study Hub to receive and review it. If accepted, it may be included in the public library. A submission is not automatically published, and Study Hub may decline or remove it.</p>
        <p>Do not include private or sensitive personal information in a resource, its description, or a suggestion. See the <a href={`${home}/privacy.html`}>Privacy Policy</a> and <a href={`${home}/copyright.html`}>Copyright Information</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Rights in resources</h2>
        <p>Rights in original Study Hub material and third-party resources remain with their respective rights holders. These terms do not transfer ownership or grant permission to reuse material. See the <a href={`${home}/copyright.html`}>Copyright Information</a> page to raise a rights concern.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. AI study tools</h2>
        <p>AI-generated explanations can be inaccurate, incomplete, or unsuitable for your course. Check them against trusted learning materials and teacher guidance; do not treat them as official examination guidance or professional advice. When you submit an AI request, the page image, question, and recent conversation context are processed by Study Hub’s AI service and Google Gemini. See the <a href={`${home}/privacy.html`}>Privacy Policy</a> before using the feature.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. External services and advertising</h2>
        <p>Some pages load or link to services operated by other organisations, including fonts, video, AI, hosting, catalogue, and advertising services. Those services have their own terms and privacy practices. Study Hub does not control their availability or policies. Google AdSense code is present on some subject pages; the handling of information by Google is described in Google’s own notices and settings.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Changes and contact</h2>
        <p>Study Hub may revise these terms as the service changes. The date above identifies the latest revision. Questions about these terms may be sent to <a href="mailto:trusteth777@gmail.com">trusteth777@gmail.com</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
